<%# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    OBJECTIVES (WP2). Task ids are fixed by CONTRACT.md S8 and must not be
    renamed -- ink packages reference them in #complete_task tags, and taskOnKO
    / concludeRequires reference them here.

    Aim chain: commit_the_team -> reach_the_control_network; then, on the
    first server-hall entry, reach_the_control_room -> take_the_attack_host ->
    end_the_sequence and trace_the_intrusion (side branch). PASS 5 scenario
    design r1 (m1): the control-room and plant aims are story-gated on
    server_hall_reached (HaX's room_entered:server_room mapping sets it and
    calls unlockAim), so the ops floor announces one aim, not three, and each
    branch is announced where its door is. Neither aim has a task that can
    complete before the server hall; an early one would be recorded and shown
    on unlock (revealAimForTask). Two of its tasks are
    required within the aim since alignment round 2 (U5), but no other aim and
    no concludeRequires entry depends on it, so it never gates the conclusion.

    Aim `status: "locked"` is presentation only -- objectives-manager.js:412 and
    :543 auto-reveal a locked parent aim when one of its tasks completes -- so a
    locked aim can never strand a task. Every task therefore ships `active`.

    The people a player can legitimately walk past (Hollis, Elena, Park) and
    the lore drops are `optional: true`. The generator hall and the keypad are
    required within trace_the_intrusion only (U5), which gates nothing, so the
    ending never depends on content the player was allowed to skip.

    mission_complete and grid_saved are set from shut_down_the_cascade's
    onComplete.setGlobal -- the terminal, never a KO-able conversation.
