          "name": "Plant Maintenance Log",
          "position": "as-type:notes_plantlog",
          "takeable": false,
          "readable": true,
          "readDisplay": "gameDisplay",
          "observations": "The plant log, chained to the wall beside the transfer switch. Every entry is initialled. The site standard is to write the keypad code in it, because the alternative is an engineer locked out of the vault at three in the morning.",
          "observationDisplay": "gameDisplay",
          "text": "BACKUP GENERATION HALL -- PLANT MAINTENANCE LOG\n\n02 JUN  Weekly load test, gensets 1-3. Pass. -- T.O.\n09 JUN  Weekly load test, gensets 1-3. Pass. -- T.O.\n15 JUN  Cable vault opened for OptiGrid cabling survey. Escorted. -- T.O.\n16 JUN  Transfer switch firmware -- vendor update applied out of window. NOT MY CALL. -- T.O.\n16 JUN  Cable vault keypad reset by OptiGrid after the survey. New code not passed to plant. Chased twice. -- T.O.\n\nSTANDING NOTE (do not remove):\n  Cable vault keypad: 2291   VOID -- see 16 JUN\n  The vault is on the plant keypad, NOT the badge system. If the badge system\n  is down you can still get in. If the keypad is down, phone Facilities and wait.",
          "puzzle_graph_role": "clue",
          "puzzle_graph_reveals": "vault_keypad_reset_by_optigrid"
        },
        {
          "_comment": "Park's sabotage target. PASS 3 (P6): its rating plate carries the vault code (last four of the serial). (P8): while Park is alive and not talked round, after the vault visit, it shows him at work; first match wins. Every variant keeps the plate line. PASS 4 round 2 (re-review F3): the plate gives the digits and the decode gives the rule; one route, drawn as an AND gate with the relay (the decode is in its itemsHeld, which the graph generator does not walk).",
          "type": "batrack",
          "id": "backup_transfer_switch",
          "name": "Backup Power Transfer Switch",
          "position": "as-type:pnw_ats",
          "takeable": false,
          "readable": true,
          <%# Blind run A fixes (M3): the plate was at the end of a long caption that the
              one-line toast cut off, so the serial (the vault PIN) never showed. It now
              opens as a dialog (readDisplay) with the plate first; a copy goes to notes. %>
          "readDisplay": "gameDisplay",
          "observations": "Rating plate riveted to the door: ATS-1, S/N 0098-<%= vault_pin %>. The automatic transfer switch, the thing that moves the building onto its own generators when the grid drops it. Somebody has already had the cover off.",
          "text": "AUTOMATIC TRANSFER SWITCH -- ATS-1\nSTATUS: ARMED / AUTO\nRating plate: ATS-1   S/N 0098-<%= vault_pin %>\n\nThe cover screws are on the floor. There is a fresh jumper across the control terminals and a length of cable coiled underneath it that is not part of the installation. Whoever left it there did not finish, and did not take their tools.",
          "textVariants": [
            {
              "condition": "globalVars.vault_entered === true && !globalVars.park_ko && globalVars.park_resolved !== 'talked'",
              "value": "AUTOMATIC TRANSFER SWITCH -- ATS-1\nSTATUS: ARMED / AUTO -- CONTROL RUN FAULT\nRating plate: ATS-1   S/N 0098-<%= vault_pin %>\n\nThe jumper across the control terminals is finished now, and the fault lamp on the control run is blinking amber. Somewhere below, the run that feeds this switch is being cut."
            }
